//? Title: A k-d tree query: inspect the branch that was actually pruned
//? Subtitle: Owned point identities, widened distances and actual visit/plane decisions
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A balanced planar k-d tree alternates median split axes and prunes subtrees
whose split plane cannot improve the incumbent distance. We begin with one
actual pruning decision, retain the original200-point query and five-nearest
result, and cover duplicates, inclusive radii and distance-range failures.
Native histories expose producing visits and post-near-subtree decisions without
replay. Measured node counts are separated from construction, trace copies and
distribution-dependent performance expectations.
)

\toc

> Read an actual pruning decision first

Use five points and query (.1,.1). The first native record type inspects a
point; the second tests a nonnull far subtree after completing the near
traversal. The diagram selects an actual pruned far child, with the recorded
plane bound and incumbent distance. It does not reconstruct another nearest
search.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kdtree_prune.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/kdtree_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <cmath>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const dm::geometry::KDTree2D tree({{0, 0}, {2, 0}, {1, 3}, {4, 2}, {-2, 1}});
    const auto t = tree.nearest_trace({.1, .1});
    std::print("| event | kind | original node | axis | actual measure | best id after | explore far |\n| " "---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.probes.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &e = t.probes[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.12f} | {} | {} |\n", i,
                   e.action == dm::geometry::KDProbeAction::Visit ? "point"
                   : "plane", e.original_index, e.axis, e.measure,
                   e.best_index_after, e.explore_far);
    }
    const auto it =
        std::find_if(t.probes.begin(), t.probes.end(), [](const auto &e) {
        return e.action == dm::geometry::KDProbeAction::FarPlane &&
            !e.explore_far;
    });
    if (it == t.probes.end())
        throw std::runtime_error("pruning witness");
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("node", {0, 0},
           std::format("Node {} axis {}", it->original_index, it->axis)).node(
        "bound", {5, 0}, std::format("Actual plane bound\n{:.5g}", it->measure)).node("best", {10, 0}, std::format("Actual best distance\n{:.5g}", it->best_distance_before)).node("decision", {15, 0}, std::format("Prune far child {}", it->child_index)).edge("node", "bound").edge("bound", "best").edge("best", "decision").save_svg("build/kdtree_prune.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| event | kind | original node | axis | actual measure | best id after | explore far |
| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| 0 | point | 2 | 0 | 3.036445290138 | 2 | false |
| 1 | point | 4 | 1 | 2.284731931759 | 4 | false |
| 2 | point | 0 | 0 | 0.141421356237 | 0 | false |
| 3 | plane | 2 | 0 | 0.900000000000 | 0 | false |
\image(figures/kdtree_prune.svg)
// result_end
\caption(An actual far-plane test excludes a subtree.)
\alttext(The recorded plane lower bound exceeds the actual incumbent distance, so the recorded nonnull far child is pruned.)

> Derive the plane lower bound

At a node splitting coordinate a at s, every point on the far side differs from
query q along that coordinate by at least |q_a−s|. Euclidean distance cannot be
smaller than one coordinate difference. Therefore, in exact geometry,

$$
|q_a-s|>d_{best}\;\Longrightarrow\;\text{far subtree cannot improve the answer}.
$$
\alttext(If the distance to the split plane exceeds the best known Euclidean distance, all points beyond that plane are farther.)

The native traversal inspects the current point, visits the near child, then
uses the updated incumbent for the far decision. It explores equality to retain
deterministic original-index ties. The tree uses median partitions and
alternates x/y; equal split coordinates are ordered by the other coordinate then
original id. Construction is expected O(n log(n+1)) work with O(n) owned nodes
and logarithmic height. Balanced height does not imply a logarithmic
nearest-query bound for every point/query distribution: worst-case all nodes can
be visited.

Distances use long-double coordinate differences and hypot, avoiding raw double
square overflow/underflow. They remain rounded metrics, not exact-real
certificates for arbitrarily close distances. Equal computed distances prefer
the earliest original input identity. Nonfinite input/query coordinates reject;
a nonfinite widened distance throws on platforms whose long double cannot hold
it.

> Retain the original200-point example

The fixture keeps mt19937 seed9001, uniform[0,20) draws and original order.
Exact distribution mapping is standard-library dependent. The query remains
(10,10), and the same tree returns its five nearest points. The plot highlights
actual nearest-query visits and the five selected neighbors; it does not imply
that every stored point was inspected.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kdtree_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/kdtree_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <cmath>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto points = dm::geometry::kd_demo_points();
    const dm::geometry::KDTree2D tree(points);
    const dm::geometry::Point2D q{10, 10};
    const auto t = tree.nearest_trace(q);
    const auto knn = tree.k_nearest(q, 5);
    std::print("| actual nearest original id | x | y | widened distance | visited nodes | pruned subtrees " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} | {} | " "{} |\n",
               t.original_index, t.point.x, t.point.y, t.distance,
               t.work.visited_nodes, t.work.pruned_subtrees);
    std::print("\n| nearest rank | x | y | widened distance |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < knn.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &p = knn[i];
        std::print("| {} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} |\n", i, p.x, p.y,
                   std::hypot(static_cast<long double>(p.x) - q.x,
                              static_cast<long double>(p.y) - q.y));
        x.push_back(p.x);
        y.push_back(p.y);
    }
    auto plot = dm::geometry::kd_trace_plot(t);
    plot.points(x, y, "five", {139, 92, 246}, 5).title("Original cloud: actual visits and five nearest").save_svg("build/kdtree_original.svg");
}
```
